# GeoVision — docker build context exclusions
#
# WHY: without this, `docker build` uploads dataset/, .venv/, node_modules/ and
# other multi-GB local artifacts into the build context on every single build.
# Keeping the context small is the single biggest build-speed win available.
#
# IMPORTANT — unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern here does NOT match at every
# depth. Docker matches each pattern against the path relative to the context
# root literally, so `models/` only ever matches a top-level `models/`
# directory; `backend/models/` needs its own line, or a `**/` prefix. Found
# the hard way building Module 16: with only the bare `models/`, `.venv/`,
# and `node_modules/` lines below (which looked complete), the build context
# was still 2.37 GB and took 15 minutes to transfer — backend/.venv,
# dashboard/node_modules, and backend/models/*.pt were all still getting
# uploaded despite each looking "already excluded."

# Version control & docs
.git/
.github/
GeoVision-Vault/
thesis/
documentation/
*.md
!README.md

# Large data & artifacts — never needed at image build time. Explicit per
# package, not a **/models/** wildcard, because ai/src/ai/models/ is a real,
# tracked Python package, not a weights directory — a wildcard would also
# catch that (same reasoning as .gitignore's own models/** rules).
dataset/
models/
outputs/
backend/models/
backend/outputs/
ai/outputs/

# Local environments and dependency caches — these appear at any depth, so
# they need the explicit **/ any-depth prefix (see note above).
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.pio/
dashboard/dist/

# Secrets — belt and braces; these must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Editor / OS
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
